# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# @axiomcode/reasoning-java — .gitignore
#
# Tracked by design: src/**, src/souffle/*.dl, src/souffle/export_manifest.tsv,
# src/templates/*.map, src/pipeline/run-souffle.sh, .claude/agents/*.md,
# package-lock.json (pinned toolchain), tsconfig.json.
# Everything below is machine-local, generated, or secret.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Dependencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules
node_modules/
# and the bare name: `node_modules/` matches a directory only, so a symlink named node_modules slips past it
node_modules
jspm_packages/
web_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/sdks
!.yarn/versions

# ── TypeScript build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# dist/ is regenerated by `npm run build` (and by the `prepare` lifecycle hook),
# so it is never a source of truth. .tsbuildinfo lands in dist/ per tsconfig,
# but the loose pattern catches stray locations too.
dist/

# ...EXCEPT inside a fixture's vendored packages. A fixture vendors a dependency whose
# PUBLISHED surface is its `dist/index.d.ts` — that copy is hand-written source, never
# build output, and the whole point of the fixture is that the manifest's `types` points
# into a directory the parser skips by name. The blanket `dist/` above silently dropped
# it: `git add -A` reported success, the file never entered the index, and the fixture
# then asserted on a package staged from nowhere. Both lines are needed — git does not
# descend into an excluded directory, so the directory itself must be re-included first.
# ...EXCEPT inside a fixture's vendored packages, in ANY language's test tree. A fixture
# vendors a dependency whose PUBLISHED surface is a checked-in `dist/index.d.ts` — that
# copy is hand-written source, never build output, and the point of the fixture is that
# the manifest's `types` points into a directory the parser skips by name.
#
# `build` and `out` are here for the same reason `dist` is: the staging code looks for a
# package's declarations in all three, so a fixture can legitimately vendor a package
# that publishes into any of them. Covering only `dist` left the identical trap set for
# the next one.
#
# Both lines per directory are needed — git does not descend into an excluded directory,
# so the directory itself must be re-included before its contents can be.
# ...and these six lines were DEAD for the whole time they existed. A pattern containing a
# slash is anchored to the directory holding this file, so `test/**/vendor/**/dist/` matches
# a TOP-LEVEL `test/` and the suites live under `graph/test/`. `git check-ignore` confirms
# it: a vendored dist under graph/test/ was still ignored by the blanket above, and the one
# such file in the index survived only because it was force-added. Case
# 60-ts-emit-helpers shipped in #813 with four files and without its `lib/dist/`, so its
# golden had been blessed against inputs that existed only in one working tree and the case
# failed for everybody else from the day it landed.
#
# The rule is stated positively instead: a fixture's INPUTS are inputs whatever they are
# called, and nothing under a cases/ or fixtures/ tree is ever build output of THIS
# repository. `test/tools/no-ignored-fixtures.sh` still enforces the invariant; it could not
# catch this one, because a file that was never added is not a file it can see.
!graph/test/**/cases/**
!graph/test/**/fixtures/**
build/
out/
lib-cov/

# ...EXCEPT the Python case that tests the parser's OWN build-output exclusion (#564).
# `build/lib/pkg` inside it is a byte-identical setuptools artifact and must stay
# checked in for the case to catch a regression; `build/__init__.py` beside it is the
# CONTROL — a legitimate source package literally named `build` — which the blanket
# `build/` rule above would otherwise drop silently, same as the vendor case above. A
# negation MUST come after the rule it excepts — gitignore is last-match-wins, and a
# negation placed before the blanket it is meant to except (as the vendor `build/`
# lines above are) is dead: the blanket re-ignores everything the exception just
# re-included.
!graph/test/python/cases/15-build-artifact-exclusion/src/build/
!graph/test/python/cases/15-build-artifact-exclusion/src/build/**
*.tsbuildinfo
.tsbuildinfo
*.d.ts.map
*.js.map

# ── Soufflé engine: per-run artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────
# run-souffle.sh stages facts into <intermediate>/souffle-facts, generates a C++
# translation of the .dl program, and links a native binary. All disposable;
# only the .dl rules are source.
souffle-facts/
souffle-program.cpp
souffle-engine-*
.souffle-gen.log
*.facts
*.dl.cpp
*.dl.o
# Compiled engine binaries (the real cache lives in ~/.cache/AxiomCode-Souffle,
# outside the repo — this guards against AXIOM_SOUFFLE_CACHE being pointed here).
.souffle-cache/
souffle-cache/

# ── Generated IR / analysis artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────
# The client/library IR (all-*.csv per src/constants/schema.ts) and the engine's
# call-graph exports are produced by the pipeline, never hand-authored.
all-*.csv
call-chain-edges.csv
call-chain-*.csv
# The bundle stage's output (src/bundle/SCHEMA.md): the database, the headered core
# tables, and the raw per-language relations it was built from.
graph.sqlite
graph.sqlite-journal
csv/
raw/
client-ir/
library-ir/
intermediate/
inter/
*-ir/
# Validation / benchmark workspaces used by the callgraph-validate and
# impact-compare agents (bytecode oracles, dynamic traces, diff reports).
oracle/
oracles/

# .NET build output. The C# ground-truth tool and the runtime instrumenter are
# real source under graph/test/csharp/, and `dotnet build` drops obj/ and bin/
# beside them. This repository had no such pattern because nothing in it was C#
# until now, and the first commit after those directories stopped matching the
# `oracle/` rule above carried 50-odd generated files, a project.assets.json and
# four binaries into the tree.
[Oo]bj/
[Bb]in/
*.user

reports/
scratch/
.scratch/
tmp/
temp/
*.oracle.csv
*.diff.csv

